    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "The smallest of the five first imports, and the one that shows the shape: 200 wire records and 14 admitted declarations, of which the theorem is one.\n\nA first draft of this note claimed our own Nat prelude `does not yet carry an order relation at all`. That was wrong and checking took one command: `nat_theorem_inventory` reports 119 theorems including `Nat.le_antisymm`, `Nat.le_total`, `Nat.le_dest` and a full `Nat.le` order theory. What is true is narrower and was verified by name: **`Nat.le_refl` itself is absent from it** (measured 2026-08-15). So this import adds a proposition we do not hold, next to an order theory we largely do -- which is the realistic shape of the import/build boundary `04-implement.md` argues about, and not the clean gap the draft asserted.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
